{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/package.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T03:47:19.034080Z","id":"f3b46ee3e6b3cc8fa0788757342f2b5bb4ee8d43a95610d7df298508c620e865","body":{"detail":"Pi's guide (node_modules/@mariozechner/pi-coding-agent/docs/packages.md, \"Dependencies\") lists Pi's core modules as peerDependencies with a \"*\" range. Pi installs an npm package with npm install -g (or --prefix), and npm 7+ installs required peers: a rehearsal of npm install -g on the packed 0.5.0 tarball added a nested @mariozechner/pi-coding-agent and its provider SDKs, 202 MB, with install-script warnings, against 328 KB and one package with the peers optional. Pi loaded the optional-peer install (no node_modules) and registered /clax and skill:clax (Pi 0.73.1, RPC get_commands). scripts/test-plugins.sh requires the peers optional.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":49},"end":{"line":60},"content_hash":"5307706a3baece49ae83f06e401003af767b2ee39a2a6afdc3f86ad518d22760"},"summary":"Required (non-optional) \"*\" peers, as Pi's docs/packages.md shows them","tags":["revisit:Pi stops providing its core modules to extensions, or its docs ask for required peers for a reason other than declaring compatibility","session:claude-code:b2fe0abc-990b-4628-b4c7-4c6d7f3f261b"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/README.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T18:52:22.666801Z","id":"30613dbc3f91aaf6a446fe9ab789a0eabfdf6616db0f53aa8e6e5c07f2e3c634","body":{"detail":"Pi has no built-in MCP support, and plugins/pi/src/clax.ts reaches only a local daemon (its token) or a clax connect remote (remote.json, a LAN http://<IP>:<port> signed with the machine key, plugins/pi/src/remote.ts), so it cannot take the bearer token POST /api/hosted/agent-tokens mints (crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs mint_token). The quickstart's Pi chip (web/quickstart/index.html install-pi) and this README send Pi users to a local Clax that publishes to clax.dev instead. A third mode taking a hosted origin and an agent token, calling the hosted REST routes with Authorization: Bearer, would let People print a Pi line too; it needs the hosted routes the tools call to accept agent tokens, and the comment loop's long-poll to work against a hosted daemon.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":70},"end":{"line":80},"content_hash":"379920979eb3becf8f50aeb112d3c3194c148cd55e0fda7d7e2d06b654515c6b"},"summary":"Let the Pi extension use a hosted Clax's agent token, so Pi connects to clax.dev as Claude Code, Codex and Grok Build do","tags":["session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
